# Omenport Vigilante (2/2): "This creature has double strike as long as you've committed a crime this turn." Cast on turn 1; on turn 3
# Bot1 Bolts Bot2's face (a crime, CR 700.13) before combat, so the Vigilante has double strike and an unblocked attack deals 2 + 2:
# Bot2 20 - 3 - 4 = 13. On turn 5 Bot1 commits no crime: no double strike (the turn-3 crime doesn't carry over), and it attacks for 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Omenport Vigilante
Lightning Bolt
Plains x2
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Omenport Vigilante.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Omenport Vigilante.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot1.Battlefield.Omenport Vigilante.Keywords = DoubleStrike
Bot1.Attack(Omenport Vigilante > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 13
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Omenport Vigilante.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Omenport Vigilante > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 11
